│ assigned to three groups of SMS, telephone and regular follow-up, respectively. Each patient was assessed before and │
│ in the first, second and third months after discharge, respectively. To collect data, the Minnesota Living with      │
│ Heart Failure Questionnaire was used. The data were analyzed with software SPSS VER19 by paired t test, repeated     │
│ measure ANOVA and curves. Finding: Twenty five patients assigned to each group. Therewere not statistically          │
│ significant differences between the quality of life of the telephone follow up before and the first, second and      │
